  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TEPLO VDOMA - Thermal Energy Program for Lifesaving Outcomes: Vital Distribution Of Materials and Aid</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtProject HOPE one of key activities is 47 Mobile Medical Units that travel to villages and settlements in over 150 communities and about 3,070 locations, providing essential medical services daily in frontline regions.&#xa0; In order to strengthen Health Outcomes, in these areas of operation Project HOPE aims to support hromadas with winterisation through the proposed interventions: providing winter energy sources and support payment of utilities bills. Project HOPE has the capacity to cover need of 2,478 households for the winter period with solid fuel. Based on list of 150 hromadas in 6 frontline regions Project HOPE is operationally present in (34 of them are areas of active fight, 99 - areas of possible fight actions), in order to ensure the most effective allocation of resources, Project HOPE will prioritize support for hromadas with the areas of active fight to cover the existing needs. Project HOPE currently operates 11 MHPSS (Mental Health and Psychosocial Support) centers across the 8 oblasts supporting more than 112,154 beneficiaries annually and Project HOPE MHPSS activities are supported in 34 hospitals by incentivized in-house and remote psychologists and case managers. To further enhance the psychological outcomes for the beneficiaries in need, Project HOPE will aid with utilities bills coverage to address holistic needs and by decreasing this financial burden aim to create a more stable and supportive environment during the winter period, ultimately contributing to lower distress and better psychosocial well-being.lt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
